2. Floor Division //
Floor division gives the whole-number quotient by removing the fractional part.
137 // 12
Output:
11
It means 137 parts can make 11 complete groups of 12.
3. Modulus %
The modulus operator gives the remainder after division.
137 % 12
Output:
5
Therefore:
12 × 11 + 5 = 137
So there are 11 complete groups and 5 remaining parts.
